     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **The problem:** Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,000 to 2,550 mg/day: 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. This is about twice that limit. It carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n- **Possible intended doses:** The order may contain a typo. It could have been meant as 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day) or 500 mg or 1000 mg twice daily. I don't want to guess.\n\nPlease have the prescribing clinician confirm the intended dose, formulation and frequency. I can enter the order once I have that, or you can give me a corrected dose. If 5,100 mg/day really is intended, a licensed prescriber will need to confirm it and document the rationale before I enter it."
      }
     ],
